मीमांसाभाष्य
मीमांसाभाष्य or मीमांसासूत्रभाष्य or शबरभाष्य or शा-<BR>बरभाष्य the oldest C. in existence on the Mīmāṃsā-<BR>sūtra, by Śabarasvāmin<BR>1) He himself refers several times to a Vṛttikāra, and mentions<BR>Bhagavān Upavarṣaḥ on 1, 1. 5, whom he designates as Bhagavān<BR>Ācāryaḥ on 2. 3, 16. The statement in Hall p. 169 must in<BR>consequence be erroneous.IO. 2--4. 1808. 1808 A.<BR>Hall p. 169. Khn. 52. K. 110. Ben. 85--100.<BR>106. 110. 113. 114. 116--19. 124. Bik. 551. Oudh<BR>1876, 16. 18. XVII, 64. 66. Burnell 81^a. Bh. 30.<BR>Poona 197. Oppert 488. 736. 2061. 3035. 3362.<BR>3868. 4066. 4254. 4935. II, 1190. 1551. 3844.<BR>4363. 4990. 7157. 7918. 9328. 9520. Rice 128.<BR>Peters. 2, 191 (fr.). 3, 391 (fr.). BP. 266 (fr.). W.<BR>1614 (fr.). 1615 (fr.). Bühler 549 (fr.).<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=ACC&page=1-457-a" target="_blank">Page1-457-a+ 45</a>]<BR>		C. NP. 1, 48.<BR>		C. Tantravārttika (q. v.) by Kumarila.<BR>		C. by Śālikanātha. IO. 422.<BR>		Arthavādacaraṇa. Ben. 99. NP. I, 30.<BR>		Tarkacaraṇa. Ben. 101. 104. NP. I, 134.<BR>		Nāmacaraṇa. NP. I, 44.<BR>		Prayojakādhyāya. NP. I, 2.<BR>		Bhāvārthacaraṇa. Ben. 95. 101. NP. I, 50. 130.<BR>		Rathaṃtaracaraṇa. Ben. 90. NP. I, 42.<BR>		Liṅgacaraṇa. Ben. 96. NP. I, 48.<BR>		Śruticaraṇa. Ben. 91. 94. 101.<BR>		Smṛticaraṇa. Ben. 90. 91. NP. I, 134.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=ACC&page=1-456,2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=acc" target="_blank">Correction</a>

