विजयपुरकथा
विजयपुरकथा ‘a short account of Vijayapur and its<BR>Mohammedan sovereigns’ Mack. 98. The same tract<BR>in 5 leaves is found in IO. 3179. Its title is Vijaya-<BR>puramahārājadhānyāṃ Dakhanīpādaśāhānāṃ vistāraḥ.<BR>This is a meagre list of the Mohammedan and Hindu<BR>rulers of Vijayapura in the Dekkan, up to the conquest<BR>by the Mlechas (the English), and was copied and<BR>no doubt composed in 1808 by Pānduraṅga, son<BR>of Rāma Jyotirvid, and great grandson of the astro-<BR>nomer Tammaṇa, who lived under Aurangzīb.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=ACC&page=1-570,1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=acc" target="_blank">Correction</a>

