शङ्करानन्द
शङ्करानन्द son of Vāñcheśa and Veṅkaṭāmbā, pupil of<BR>Ānandātman, guru of Sāyaṇa (Oxf. 222^a):<BR>		Ātmapurāṇa or Upaniṣadratna, the substance of<BR>a number of Upaniṣads, in verse.<BR>		He wrote dīpikās on the following Upaniṣads:<BR>Atharvaśikhā, Atharvaśiras, Atharvaśīrṣa, Amṛ-<BR>tanāda, Amṛtabindu, Āruṇī, Īśāvāsya, Aitareya,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=ACC&page=1-629-b" target="_blank">Page1-629-b+ 46</a>]<BR>Kāṭhaka, Keneṣita, Kaivalya, Kauṣītaka, Ga-<BR>rbha, Chāndogya, Jābāla, Taittirīya, Nārāyaṇa,<BR>Nṛsiṃhatāpanīya, Paramahaṃsa, Praśna, Brahman,<BR>Brahmavallī, Mahopaniṣad, Māṇḍūkya, Muṇḍaka,<BR>Śvetāśvatara, Haṃsa.<BR>		Bhagavadgītātātparyabodhinī.<BR>		Yatyanuṣṭhānapaddhati.<BR>		Śivasahasranāmaṭīkā.<BR>		Sarvapurāṇasāra.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=ACC&page=1-629,1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=acc" target="_blank">Correction</a>

