केशवदैवज्ञ|केशवदैवज्ञः
केशव दैवज्ञ son of Kamalākara and pupil of Vaidya-<BR>nātha. He was father of Ananta (Kālanirṇayāva-<BR>bodha), Gaṇeśa (Grahalāghava etc.), and Rāma, the<BR>father of Nṛsiṃha (Grahakaumudī, Grahadīpikā). His<BR>son Gaṇeśa mentions in the C. on the Muhūrtatattva<BR>the following works of Keśava:<BR>		Kāyasthādidharmapaddhati, Grahakautuka, Jāta-<BR>kapaddhati and C., Tājakapaddhati, Tithisiddhi,<BR>Muhūrtatattva, Siddhānte Upapattipāṭhanicaya,<BR>See Gaṇakataraṅgiṇī by Sudhākara in Paṇḍit<BR>XIV, p. 173. Sudhākara adds: Kuṇḍāṣṭaka-<BR>lakṣaṇa, Gaṇitadīpikā, Varṣagranthasiddhi<BR>(Siddhantavāsanāpāṭha).<BR>		The Jātakapaddhati is also called Keśavī. Keśavī<BR>bṛhatī B. 4, 166. Laghvī and C. by Viśva-<BR>nātha. K. 224. See Jātakakeśavī.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=ACC&page=2-025,1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=acc" target="_blank">Correction</a>

